<title>ESTONIA: Estonian Hansapank talks on 15 mln DEM EBRD loan.</title>
<headline>Estonian Hansapank talks on 15 mln DEM EBRD loan.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Estonian bank Hansapank on Friday said it was working on a project to take a 15 million mark subordinated loan from the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD).</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement the loan would have a maturity of 10 years and would increase own funds for the purporse of calculating capital adequacy without the need to issue new shares.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the bank said a date for the loan signature has not been signed yet but agency Baltic News Service (BNS) said the EBRD would discuss it on March 25.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
